        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "60d5e163-1813-5dad-87b3-c16d7ac4e5f0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charlie Walker, George D. Hay, Aubrey Otis Hampton\n- Organizations: Grand Ole Opry, Country Radio DJ Hall of Fame, WSM\n- Places: Copeville, Texas, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Songs and Albums: \"Little Old Wine Drinker Me\", \"Wine, Woman & Walker\"\n- Concepts: Hampton's hump, Hampton's line\n\nFacts:\n- Aubrey Otis Hampton was born in 1900 in Copeville, Texas, and he was an American radiologist remembered for describing Hampton's hump and Hampton's line.\n- The Grand Ole Opry was founded on November 28, 1925, in Nashville, Tennessee, by George D. Hay as a one-hour radio \"barn dance\" on WSM.\n- Charlie Walker was born on November 2, 1926, in Copeville, Texas, and he was an American country musician.\n- Aubrey Otis Hampton died in 1955.\n- Charlie Walker first released the song \"Little Old Wine Drinker Me\" in 1966 on the album \"Wine, Woman & Walker\".\n- Charlie Walker held membership in the Grand Ole Opry from 1967.\n- Charlie Walker was inducted into the Country Radio DJ Hall of Fame in 1981.\n- Charlie Walker died on September 12, 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5e47ef06-7bb0-5824-a75b-385ee0adaabb",
        "text": "Page: Charlie Walker (musician). Sentence: Charlie Walker (November 2, 1926 – September 12, 2008)  was an American country musician born in Copeville, Texas.\nPage: Charlie Walker (musician). Sentence: He held membership in the Grand Ole Opry from 1967, and was inducted into the Country Radio DJ Hall of Fame in 1981.\nPage: Grand Ole Opry. Sentence: The Grand Ole Opry is a weekly country-music stage concert in Nashville, Tennessee, which was founded on November 28, 1925, by George D. Hay as a one-hour radio \"barn dance\" on WSM.\nPage: Little Old Wine Drinker Me. Sentence: \"Little Old Wine Drinker Me\" is a song that was first released by Charlie Walker in 1966, on the album \"Wine, Woman & Walker\".\nPage: Aubrey Otis Hampton. Sentence: Aubrey Otis Hampton (1900, Copeville, Texas – 1955) was an American radiologist remembered for describing Hampton's hump and Hampton's line.",
